[18:21:55] I redrew the boat pose figure as a Solo48 model. It validates as `valid` with no warnings, and all four files are saved in `new-pipeline-test/output_png/20260929-1814-boat-pose-upward-reach/`.

**Subject:** a side-view stick figure in yoga boat pose (navasana). It balances on its hip at the bottom of a V, with the legs raised up to the right, the torso leaning back to the upper left, and the arms reaching up and forward in front of the head.

**Keyshape:** SQUARE, the one the metrics suggested. It now touches all four edges of its box:
- head: left edge at x=6, top at y=6
- legs tip: right edge at x=42
- hip: bottom at y=42

**Construction:**
- **Legs:** one line from the hip (19,42) to (42,19), at 45°.
- **Lower torso:** leans back about 34°, close to the trace's lean.
- **Neck:** a short vertical stroke from (11,30) up to (11,24).
- **Head:** a circle of radius 5 centred at (11,11), directly above the neck.
- **Arms:** one line from the shoulder (11,30) to (31,10), parallel to the legs.

I chose the longer arms after comparing the drawing at 48 px in light and dark themes. With shorter arms (ending at (27,14)), the shoulder corner looked like an arrowhead.

**Metric issues:**

| Issue | Status |
|---|---|
| Clearance: head too close to the arms and to the legs/torso line (3.6 units, need 8) | Fixed. The head now clears the arms by 8.4. |
| Head gap (3.54, need exactly 8) | Fixed. Exactly 8 units from head to neck (a 4-unit visible gap). |
| Head hole 2.91 wide (need 6) | Fixed. A radius-5 head leaves a 6-unit hole. |
| SQUARE only 86% filled vertically | Fixed. Every edge of the box is reached. |
| Trace stroke width (info) | Redrawn at stroke 4, and every gap was measured at 4. |

**Two deliberate changes from the trace:**
- **Head position:** the head sits upright on its own vertical neck instead of on the slanted torso line. The validator can't confirm an exact 8-unit head gap on a diagonal. My first version did that, and it came back `review` rather than `valid`.
- **Arm height:** the arm tip no longer rises above the head. With the shoulder only 6 units below the neck, steeper arms can't stay 8 units clear of the head.

**References:** I followed the shared human reference for the circular head, single-stroke limbs and 4-unit head gap. There was no useful Lucide match for a yoga pose.

As you asked, I didn't register the module, touch `published/`, or run the build or gallery updates.

Files are in `new-pipeline-test/output_png/20260929-1814-boat-pose-upward-reach/`:
- `boat_pose_upward_reach_redraw.py`
- `boat-pose-upward-reach_redraw.svg`
- `boat-pose-upward-reach_redraw.png`
- `boat-pose-upward-reach_redraw-48.png`

